<main>
  <h1>About DailyKitBox</h1>
  <p class="lead">DailyKitBox is a free online toolbox built around one idea: everyday tools shouldn't require an account, a subscription, or your files leaving your device.</p>

  <h2>Why We Built This</h2>
  <p>Most people don't need a full software suite to merge a couple of PDFs, check a mortgage payment, or work out a tip. They need a tool that opens fast, does one job well, and gets out of the way. Too many "free" tools online bury that simplicity behind sign-up walls, watermarks, upload limits, or hidden file storage. DailyKitBox was built to remove all of that friction.</p>

  <h2>How Our Tools Work</h2>
  <p>Every PDF tool on this site — Merge, Split, Delete Pages, Images to PDF, the Office Converter and the Branding & Security toolkit — runs entirely inside your browser. Your files are read, processed and merged locally on your own device using modern web technology. Nothing is ever uploaded to a server, which means your documents stay private by design, not by policy.</p>
  <p>Our calculators — Age, Tip, Mortgage, Word Counter and others — follow the same principle: instant, accurate results with no data collection beyond what's needed to show you the answer.</p>

  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>50+ Tools</h3>
      <p>PDF utilities, calculators, generators and everyday web tools, all in one place.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>No Sign-Up</h3>
      <p>Every tool works the moment you open it. No accounts, no email required.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Private By Design</h3>
      <p>File-based tools process everything locally in your browser — nothing is uploaded.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Always Free</h3>
      <p>No premium tier, no watermarks, no artificial limits on how much you can use.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Who's Behind DailyKitBox</h2>
  <p>DailyKitBox is built and maintained independently, with each tool designed, tested and refined one at a time. New tools are added regularly based on what people actually search for and need in day-to-day work.</p>

  <h2>Get In Touch</h2>
  <p>Have a tool idea, found a bug, or just want to say hello? We'd like to hear from you.</p>
